WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.750
Starting in 2003, American Chopper dominated
reality television for ten years, giving a

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:10.690
look at the inside workings of Orange County
Choppers with a mix of competition and drama

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:14.260
that provided a model for all reality shows
that have followed.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:19.440
Unlike most so-called reality shows, though,
the fighting, cursing, crying, welding, and

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.919
painting on American Chopper was real.

00:00:21.919 --> 00:00:25.779
Here's a look at the untold truth of American
Chopper.

00:00:25.779 --> 00:00:27.369
Drinking and welding

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:32.840
In his book The Ride of a Lifetime, Paul Teutul,
Sr. discusses his 15-year drug and alcohol

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:38.220
addiction, which ended when he went to rehab
on the advice of his wife in 1985.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.220
He wrote,

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.220
"Somehow, she talked me into going into rehab,
something I thought I'd never do.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:45.860
But I wanted to have one last good drunk.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:49.250
So the day before I was set to go into rehab,
I got totally plastered.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:54.430
I drank a half-gallon of wine, a pint of brandy,
and I took six Valiums."

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:59.440
While Paul Sr. was ultimately able to stop
his drinking, his sons Mikey and Paul Jr.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:04.809
both had issues with drugs and alcohol, with
Paul Jr. going to rehab at age 16.

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:07.070
Father-son feud

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:11.830
Fights between the Pauls were a regular occurrence
on the show, driving much of the onscreen

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:12.830
drama.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:17.990
But the most heated argument ever captured
on camera happened in 2009, when a chair-throwing

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:27.200
Paul Junior was dressed down by his father
for sleeping on the job and showing up late.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:32.700
It seemed like the perfect reality TV show
plotline — but this wasn't scripted drama.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.899
Paul Senior actually fired his son, which
opened a whole new can of worms, because the

00:01:36.899 --> 00:01:40.610
show's contract stipulated that Paul Junior
had to be involved.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:45.909
The network, TLC, filed a notice of default,
forcing Paul Senior to bring Paul Junior back

00:01:45.909 --> 00:01:50.600
as a contractor so he could stay on the show
without technically working for his dad.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.780
But then things got even uglier.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:57.149
The new contract had a clause that allowed
Paul Senior to buy out his son's stake in

00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:58.640
Orange County Choppers.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.340
Junior refused, and dad sued him for a million
dollars.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:06.729
Junior took him to court and won, retaining
his stake in the company, but the two eventually

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:11.290
decided it would be better for their relationship
if they just stopped working together entirely.

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:14.129
A tragic accident

00:02:14.129 --> 00:02:18.890
In 2010, Paul Junior branched out and opened
his own custom motorcycle shop, Paul Junior

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:19.890
Designs.

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:22.260
But the business began under a dark cloud.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:26.939
Shortly after opening, a man contracted by
the building's owner to repair the roof fell

00:02:26.939 --> 00:02:27.939
and died.

00:02:27.939 --> 00:02:30.209
In a statement, Paul Junior said,

00:02:30.209 --> 00:02:34.989
"This was a tragic accident and, although
I've never met this man, my deepest condolences

00:02:34.989 --> 00:02:38.079
and prayers go out to his family and friends."

00:02:38.079 --> 00:02:39.079
Wedding snub

00:02:39.079 --> 00:02:44.940
In 2010, Paul Junior married Rachael Biester,
a model he'd met on an episode of American

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:45.940
Chopper.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:50.799
In advance of their wedding, the couple appeared
on TLC's show Say Yes to the Dress, and even

00:02:50.799 --> 00:02:55.909
met with a chef from TLC's Cake Boss to really
hammer home the fact that TLC pretty much

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.330
owns these people.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:01.930
One person, however, did not attend Paul and
Rachael's wedding: Paul Senior, who skipped

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:04.549
the event even though he was invited.

00:03:04.549 --> 00:03:05.739
Ouch.

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:06.790
Case of stolen idea

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:13.360
In 2014, a Florida man named Christ Tavantzis
sued the two Pauls and Orange County Choppers

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:14.819
for copyright infringement.

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:19.390
Tavantzis, who suffered from polio and was
wheelchair-bound until his death in February

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:24.719
2016, claimed that he pitched the idea of
a handicap-accessible, three-wheel motorcycle

00:03:24.719 --> 00:03:27.840
to members of the shop at a bike show in 2008.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:31.989
Tavantzis contended that this bike, which
the American Chopper team built at the beginning

00:03:31.989 --> 00:03:37.060
of 2010 in conjunction with the Christopher
&amp; Dana Reeve Foundation, was a ripoff of his

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:40.049
original idea, for which Tavantzis held a
patent.

00:03:40.049 --> 00:03:47.390
"I honestly mean from the bottom of my heart
that we're are honored to do this bike.

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:52.159
It's all about giving back, so we're doing
this."

00:03:52.159 --> 00:03:57.739
As of the making of this video, the case is
still making its way through the court system.

00:03:57.739 --> 00:03:59.390
Sidekicks gone wild

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:03.459
While his father and brother were settling
their differences onscreen and in court, younger

00:04:03.459 --> 00:04:08.090
son Mikey shifted his energies from Orange
County Choppers to other schemes.

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:13.420
In November 2010, he opened Wolf Gang Gallery,
an art gallery that showcased, among other

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:14.610
works, his own paintings.

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:19.310
A year after he opened the gallery, Mikey
launched a line of gourmet pasta sauces under

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:23.729
the company name FarQueue Products, which
carried flavors like Porcine Orgy Sausage

00:04:23.729 --> 00:04:24.729
Supreme.

00:04:24.729 --> 00:04:28.569
One of the show's other loveable sidekicks
didn't have such a pleasant end to his time

00:04:28.569 --> 00:04:30.380
with Orange County Choppers.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:34.650
Shop-hand Cody Connelly was a regular in the
show's early days, and at one point was given

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:37.690
a chopper for all his hard work, which he
helped design.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:44.360
However, Cody later filed a lawsuit for $250,000
in damages, claiming he never received the

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:48.850
chopper, and that Orange County Choppers continued
to use his likeness on promotional materials

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:50.530
after he'd left the company.

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:54.850
He eventually settled out of court and returned
to the show — but working for Paul Junior

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.470
instead.

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:57.889
Rumors and lies

00:04:57.889 --> 00:05:01.880
In recent years, Orange County Choppers has
been dogged by persistent rumors that the

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:05.460
company is in dire financial straits and headed
for foreclosure.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:09.289
When word got out that their headquarters
was being sold, Paul Senior had to go on the

00:05:09.289 --> 00:05:12.120
radio to assure fans that they were doing
fine.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:16.220
Around the same time as the foreclosure rumors
started swirling, strange reports surfaced

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:19.759
suggesting Paul Senior had died in a motorcycle
accident.

00:05:19.759 --> 00:05:25.910
According to Snopes.com, on April 18, 2016,
the website Iron Demons doctored a real article

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:30.050
about another man's death in a motorcycle
crash in Louisiana to make it look like it

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:31.509
was Paul Sr.'s death.

00:05:31.509 --> 00:05:36.139
The rumors went viral, prompting Orange County
Choppers to post a rebuttal on Facebook.

00:05:36.139 --> 00:05:41.040
The show may be dead for now, but its stars,
at least, are still alive and kicking.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.550
Thanks for watching!

